DOCUMENTATION:
  PURPOSE:  handshaker <-> SNANA magcor cross-check
  INTENT:   One LIBID, exactly one observation per band, at a single MJD.
            The SAME simlib feeds two sims that differ ONLY in the kcor:
              (A) reference (nominal filters)  + K-star mag system
              (B) ice filters                  + K-star mag system
            magcor(band) = mag_A(band) - mag_B(band)  [from SIM_FLUXCAL]
  NOTES:
    - Noiseless truth (SIM_FLUXCAL) is used, so ZPT/SKY/PSF values are
      placeholders; they must only be IDENTICAL between the two runs.
    - MWEBV = 0 and no dust model (set in the sim-input, step 6).
    - Trest per obs is controlled in the sim-input via PEAKMJD (step 5):
          Trest = (MJD_obs - PEAKMJD) / (1 + z)
      With MJD_obs = 61010 below, PEAKMJD = 61000 and z gives Trest.
      e.g. PEAKMJD 61010 -> Trest 0 (peak);  61000, z=0 -> Trest +10 d.
DOCUMENTATION_END:

SURVEY:   ROMAN
FILTERS:  RZYJHFK
TELESCOPE: ROMAN
PIXSIZE:  0.11

BEGIN LIBGEN

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
LIBID: 1
RA: 9.0  DECL: -44.0  NOBS: 7  MWEBV: 0.000  PIXSIZE: 0.11
FIELD: TEST
#                                                  PSF1 PSF2 P2/1
#     MJD      IDEXPT FLT GAIN RDNOISE SKYSIG     (pix)(pix)(ratio)  ZPTAVG ZPTERR  MAG
S:  61010.000    1    R   1.0   5.0     10.0       1.50 0.00 0.00    32.00  0.005  -99.0
S:  61010.000    2    Z   1.0   5.0     10.0       1.50 0.00 0.00    32.00  0.005  -99.0
S:  61010.000    3    Y   1.0   5.0     10.0       1.50 0.00 0.00    32.00  0.005  -99.0
S:  61010.000    4    J   1.0   5.0     10.0       1.50 0.00 0.00    32.00  0.005  -99.0
S:  61010.000    5    H   1.0   5.0     10.0       1.50 0.00 0.00    32.00  0.005  -99.0
S:  61010.000    6    F   1.0   5.0     10.0       1.50 0.00 0.00    32.00  0.005  -99.0
